Subject: [PATCH] mediafoundation: decline only the WinRT half when GstWinRt is unavailable

On a desktop Windows target BOTH partition probes succeed: WINAPI_PARTITION_DESKTOP and
WINAPI_PARTITION_APP are true at the same time, so winapi_desktop and winapi_app are both
set and the plugin is meant to build both halves.

The WinRT half needs the GstWinRt library from gst-libs/gst/winrt, and that library is
MSVC-ONLY by upstream's own decision:

    gst-libs/gst/winrt/meson.build:
        if cxx.get_id() != 'msvc'
          subdir_done()

So on any other toolchain gstwinrt_dep can never be found, and the block patched here then
abandons THE WHOLE SUBDIRECTORY -- taking the desktop half with it, which needs nothing from
WinRT and would have built perfectly. With mediafoundation left at 'auto' that happens in
complete silence: the result is a gstreamer with no mfh264enc, no mfh265enc, no mfaacenc and
no Media Foundation decoders, and nothing anywhere saying why.

The two halves are not alternatives, and the code three lines further down already knows it:
`if winapi_desktop` adds the desktop sources independently. Only the app branch conflates
"the UWP sources cannot be built" with "nothing can be built".

What the WinRT half actually contains is gstmfcapturewinrt.cpp and mediacapturewrapper.cpp --
UWP camera capture, which a desktop build has no use for. Every encoder and decoder lives in
the unconditional source list, which is why declining that half costs nothing here.

So: when GstWinRt is missing and the desktop partition is available, clear winapi_app and
carry on. The error is kept for the only case in which nothing can be built -- no desktop
partition either. GST_MF_WINAPI_APP follows winapi_app, so the generated config stays honest.

MSVC is unaffected: there gstwinrt builds, gstwinrt_dep is found, and both halves are taken
exactly as before.
---
diff --git a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/mediafoundation/meson.build b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/mediafoundation/meson.build
--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/mediafoundation/meson.build
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/mediafoundation/meson.build
@@ -124,8 +124,9 @@ if not winapi_desktop and not winapi_app
   error('Neither Desktop partition nor App partition')
 endif
 
-if winapi_app
-  if not gstwinrt_dep.found()
+if winapi_app and not gstwinrt_dep.found()
+  # Nothing can be built only when the desktop partition is unavailable too.
+  if not winapi_desktop
     if mf_option.enabled()
       error('The mediafoundation plugin was enabled explicitly, but GstWinRt library is unavailable')
     else
@@ -133,6 +134,13 @@ if winapi_app
     endif
   endif
 
+  # GstWinRt is MSVC-only upstream, so on any other toolchain this half can never be
+  # built. Decline just this half: the desktop plugin below is unaffected, and all it
+  # costs is UWP camera capture, which a desktop build cannot use anyway.
+  winapi_app = false
+endif
+
+if winapi_app
   mf_sources += mf_app_sources
   mf_lib_deps += [runtimeobject_lib, gstwinrt_dep]
 endif
